        Review these 15 detailed conversion scenarios with explicit clock and calendar date breakdowns:
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 1: Midnight GMT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>00:00 GMT → 09:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            When a new calendar day starts at midnight in Greenwich (00:00 GMT), citizens in Japan are opening morning offices at 09:00 AM JST on the exact same date.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 2: Early Morning GMT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>03:00 GMT → 12:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            An early 03:00 AM GMT automated build aligns with 12:00 PM (noon) JST lunch hour in Tokyo.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 3: Morning Dispatch</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>06:00 GMT → 15:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            A 06:00 AM GMT dispatch arrives at 15:00 (3:00 PM) JST during mid-afternoon office hours in Osaka.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 4: Mid-Morning GMT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>09:00 GMT → 18:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            When London offices open at 09:00 AM GMT, Japanese teams are wrapping up their business day at 18:00 (6:00 PM) JST.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 5: Noon GMT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>12:00 GMT → 21:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            12:00 PM (noon) GMT translates to 21:00 (9:00 PM) JST in the evening across Japan.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 6: Mid-Afternoon GMT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">
            <strong>14:00 GMT → 23:00 JST (Same Day)</strong><br />
            14:00 (2:00 PM) GMT equals 23:00 (11:00 PM) JST, the final hour before midnight in Japan on the same date.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent);">Example 7: Midnight Rollover Threshold</h3>
