        <strong>No. Japan does NOT currently observe seasonal Daylight Saving Time (DST).</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Although Japan temporarily implemented daylight saving time between 1948 and 1951 during the post-WWII Allied occupation, the practice was unpopular among agricultural workers and the general public, leading to its complete repeal in 1952. Since 1951, Japan has operated on a permanent, static <strong>UTC+9</strong> offset all 365 days of the year.
      </p>
